  What I'm deliberately [3mnot[0m building: no analytics sink, no consent banner, no logout UI, no change to [38;5;153msrc/[39m (it's
  CommonJS and unrelated to the page). The id is stored and readable; sending it anywhere is a later decision.

  [1mTooling, alongside the architecture.[0m This repo has no test runner, no linter, and no formatter, and tooling is
  cheapest to add before the code exists rather than after. The fork matters because it decides whether the TTL and
  overwrite rules ship with proof or with my say-so.

  - [1m[38;5;153mnode:test[39m only[0m — Node's built-in runner, zero dependencies, no [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m changes beyond a [38;5;153mtest[39m script. The
    factory design means [38;5;153midentity.js[39m is directly testable with a fake storage object. Buys real tests on the expiry and
    overwrite logic, which is the part most likely to be subtly wrong.
  - [1m[38;5;153mnode:test[39m + Biome[0m — adds lint and format in a single dependency for a two-file codebase. Buys consistency, costs you
    a [38;5;153mnode_modules[39m in a repo that currently has none.
  - [1mNeither[0m — I verify by hand and describe what I checked. Fastest path to the code; the TTL and overwrite behavior
    ship unproven.
